{"_v":1,"id":"twelfth-night-1998","bd":{"positive":4,"mixed":1,"negative":0},"rv":[{"cn":"Mark Kennedy","o":"Associated Press","s":82,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"http://news.yahoo.com/review-mark-rylance-shines-2-shakespeare-parts-030209527.html;_ylt=A2KJ3CQWSYBSbyMAQYPQtDMD","q":"They bring the plays alive, brilliantly and made immediate"},{"cn":"Linda Winer","o":"Newsday","s":75,"b":"Positive","t":1,"u":"http://www.newsday.com/entertainment/theater/twelfth-night-and-richard-iii-review-top-notch-event-theater-1.6407270","q":"'Twelfth Night' is the centerpiece that gives the most chances for nuanced sexuality and comic delight."},{"cn":"Joe Dziemianowicz","o":"New York Daily News","s":84,"b":"Rave","t":2,"u":"http://www.nydailynews.com/entertainment/music-arts/twelfth-night-richard-iii-theater-reviews-article-1.1511003","q":"Rylance is surrounded by a sublime company, who move seamlessly between the plays."},{"cn":"Robert Feldberg","o":"NorthJersey.com","s":74,"b":"Positive","t":2,"u":"http://www.northjersey.com/arts_entertainment/theater/231392511_Theater_review___Twelfth_Night__and__Richard_III_.html?page=all","q":"Rylance finds a way to go the extra yard as Olivia"},{"cn":"Joe Dziemianowicz","o":"New York Theatre Guide","s":64,"b":"Mixed","t":2,"u":"https://www.newyorktheatreguide.com/reviews/twelfth-night-review-shakespeare-in-the-park","q":"Between bicycles, bongs, beatboxing, and buffoonery cranked to the max, playfulness rules in director Saheem Ali’s contemporary staging. That’s a viable approach to this 400-plus-year-old play — it’s a romantic comedy, after all. Nonetheless, like the richest rom-coms, Twelfth Night can cut deep when it matters most."}],"au":{"score":83,"designation":"Liking","sources":{"mz":{"s":83,"c":312,"sr":4.1}}},"pd":"1998-06-19","ca":[{"n":"Kim Awon","r":"Lady in Olivia's house"},{"n":"Philip Bosco","r":"Malvolio"},{"n":"Kevin Daniels","r":"Officer"},{"n":"Adam Dannheisser","r":"Officer"},{"n":"Jack Davidson","r":"Priest"},{"n":"Ryan D